summary:
  Escape closes the larger cover and is then passed on to the page behind
  it.

history:
  The Playing page answers Escape itself: it goes back to the station
  list, and from there the popup closes. With the larger cover up, one
  Escape has to mean "put the picture back" and nothing more, or closing
  the picture also throws the listener off the page they were looking at.
  The larger view takes the key. This mutant lets it through.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CoverTouch.qml

find:
                  touch.closeLarger()
                  event.accepted = true
              } else if (event.key === Qt.Key_Tab || event.key === Qt.Key_Backtab) {

replace:
                  touch.closeLarger()
                  event.accepted = false
              } else if (event.key === Qt.Key_Tab || event.key === Qt.Key_Backtab) {

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_covertouch.qml::test_the_keyboard_shows_the_cover_larger_and_escape_puts_it_back.
  Line-neutral.
